The issue was that `LiveRender.position_cursor` in `rich/live_render.py` would return a `Control` object that performed a carriage return and erased the current line even when the height of the renderable was 0. This caused `Live` to accidentally delete the last line of printed console output when it was empty.

I modified `rich/live_render.py` to return an empty `Control()` if `self._shape` is `None` or if the height of the renderable is 0. This ensures that cursor manipulation only occurs when the `Live` region actually occupies space on the screen.

